From c9c763e4c23ca885b2d8e05338149131a53696e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Paprocki <hi@rpaprocki.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:38:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 15/28] ui: site defaults and hints for the server fields, a
 reference for the Other section

Custom Server: RDGEN_DEFAULT_PORT, RDGEN_DEFAULT_URL_LINK,
RDGEN_DEFAULT_DOWNLOAD_LINK and RDGEN_DEFAULT_COMPANY prefill the
remaining fields (validated like the others). Each field says what it
changes in the client. The update URL is downloaded and run by installed
Windows clients (updater.rs, update_progress.dart), so the hint says it
must be a direct installer link.

Other: the section explains the key=value format, default vs override,
and that a line replaces the matching control. A reference table built
from RustDesk's advanced-settings documentation (client_settings.json:
140 options, values, defaults, short descriptions, checked against the
client source) can be filtered and adds a line to either box. Both boxes
are checked as you type: lines without '=', invalid names, top-level
keys that have no effect there, unknown keys, values outside Y/N-style
choices, duplicates, keys a form control already sets, and keys present
in both boxes.

Fix: "Deny LAN discovery" and "Automatically close incoming sessions"
wrote enable-lan-discovery and allow-auto-disconnect at the top level of
custom.txt. The client keeps top-level keys in HARD_SETTINGS but reads
these two through Config::get_option(), so the boxes had no effect. When
ticked they now go into the default or override map chosen for the
permissions.
